cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Genna Clash or its question bank in teaching, research, an event or another project, please cite it
  as below.
type: software
title: "Genna Clash: A bilingual multiplayer team quiz inspired by Genna, the Ethiopian Christmas game"
abstract: >-
  Genna Clash (Amharic: የጎጃም ገና, "Genna of Gojjam") is a free, real-time multiplayer quiz game for classrooms and
  families, inspired by Genna, the traditional stick-and-ball game played in the Ethiopian highlands at Christmas.
  Two teams, Red and Green, answer the same 15-second questions; fast correct answers push the ball towards the
  other team's goal. It offers 120 questions in English and Amharic across four categories (math, science, Amharic
  words, and Ethiopia and Gojjam), a teacher mode that filters questions by school grade (3–8) and category, original
  SVG/CSS artwork and browser-generated sound. It runs as a static web page on GitHub Pages with Firebase Realtime
  Database and anonymous sign-in, so players need no accounts.
